From db4198ee4e97937bac9ed94d479c203d4e9ca925 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:27:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Review routing: a downstream review card may declare
 its implementer models

Problem: 2026-11-19, review card t_7da7c164e7b1d000 of PR #3633 gave up twice: "Review model resolution failed:
Downstream review implementer evidence is unavailable". PR #3633 was written in a Claude Code session.

Why 1: since 3249911ef27 `resolve_review_model` refuses a downstream review (title "Independent ... review") when
`implementer_models` finds no implementer, so a reviewer is never chosen blind and never on the implementer's model.
Why 2: `implementer_models` reads implementers only from linked source cards (pins and run routes) and the creator
card.
Why 3: a change written outside the board (a Claude Code session landing through `hermes-core-wt ship`) has no
source card; ship files the review card from a CLI with no creator and no links.
Root (happened): the provenance rule had no input for work that no card performed.
Root (not caught): the fail-closed tests covered missing and evicted source cards, not reviews of card-less work.

Fix: `declared_implementers(body)` reads one line `<!-- implementer-models: a, b -->` from a downstream review
card's body; `implementer_models` adds those models for downstream cards. Concrete ids only: a class selector or a
malformed entry voids the whole declaration (nothing is declared). Linked and declared implementers are both
excluded. A card that is not a downstream review ignores the line. `hermes-core-wt ship` writes the line from the
PR commits' Co-Authored-By trailers (state change, separate PR).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_review_declared_implementers.py (the parser's accepted and void forms; a
declared review has evidence; an undeclared one with no source still fails closed through resolve_review_model;
declared and linked models are both excluded; a non-review card's declaration is ignored).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
